  "result": "`slugify(text)` is now implemented in `src/strings.js`, and I added 8 tests for it in `test/strings.test.js`. `npm test` passes with all 10 tests, the 2 existing ones and the 8 new ones.\n\nIt applies your rules in order:\n- **đ/Đ:** replaced with `d` first, since they don't decompose into a base letter plus an accent.\n- **Diacritics:** removed by splitting each letter from its accent marks and dropping the marks.\n- **Lowercase and separators:** the text is lowercased, then every run of characters outside a-z and 0-9 becomes one hyphen.\n- **Edges:** leading and trailing hyphens are trimmed.\n- **Length:** the result is cut to 50 characters, and any hyphen left at the end of the cut is removed.\n\nThe tests cover:\n- Basic input.\n- Vietnamese text including đ.\n- Other Latin accents.\n- Collapsing runs and trimming hyphens.\n- Empty and symbol-only input, which both return an empty string.\n- Cutting at 50 characters, including a cut that would otherwise end on a hyphen.",
